# Reviews and reports are dated records, not repo prose. Reformatting a review would
# change the line numbers its own findings cite, and every queue item cites them too;
# a report describes what one run did and is finished the day it is written.
#
# `test/docs.test.ts` draws the same boundary for the figures it checks, and for the
# same reason: a document that states what was true then must not be corrected to
# match now. This file listed only `docs/reviews`, so the two disagreed about
# `docs/reports` -- which is exactly the drift the tests here exist to catch.
docs/reviews
docs/reports
